            <fr:title text="Field">Field</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
A field is a set <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F]]></fr:tex> together with two binary operations <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[+]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\times ]]></fr:tex> on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F]]></fr:tex> st <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(F,+)]]></fr:tex> is an <fr:link href="/def-0002/" title="Abel Group" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-0002/" display-uri="def-0002" type="local">abelian group</fr:link> (identity is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[0]]></fr:tex>) and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(F-\{0\},\times )]]></fr:tex> is also an abelian group such that
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[a\times (b+c)=a\times  b+a\times  c,\forall  a,b,c\in  F]]></fr:tex></html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
